e of device replacement than random cell faults.", "basis": "Row and column faults affect many addresses and can disable large memory regions; field maintenance often flags repetitive row/column errors.", "fields": ["fault_mode_row_1h", "fault_mode_row_15m", "fault_mode_column_1h", "fault_mode_column_15m", "fault_row_num_1h", "fault_row_num_15m", "fault_column_num_1h", "fault_column_num_15m"], "expected_direction": "higher_in_failing", "falsified_if": "Failing devices do not exhibit elevated row/column fault counts compared with healthy devices."}, {"id": "H5", "mechanism": "Bank-level faults indicate a more severe structural defect than cell-level faults.", "basis": "Bank-level errors suggest shared circuitry failure and can affect larger memory regions.", "fields": ["fault_mode_bank_1h", "fault_mode_bank_15m"], "expected_direction": "higher_in_failing", "falsified_if": "Bank fault counts do not distinguish failing from healthy devices."}, {"id": "H6", "mechanism": "Shorter inter-burst or inter-DQ intervals signal accelerating instability rather than isolated random errors.", "basis": "Decreasing time between errors suggests a progressive physical defect; isolated errors are more likely environmental.", "fields": ["max_burst_interval_1h", "max_burst_interval_15m", "max_dq_interval_1h", "max_dq_interval_15m"], "expected_direction": "lower_in_failing", "falsified_if": "Failing devices have longer or similar maximum intervals than healthy devices, showing no temporal clustering."}, {"id": "H7", "mechanism": "CE storms (sudden bursts of many CEs) precede hard failures.", "basis": "Storm events indicate a rapid degradation phase and are commonly observed before memory faults.", "fields": ["ce_storm_count_1h", "ce_storm_count_15m", "error_burst_count_1h", "error_burst_count_15m"], "expected_direction": "higher_in_failing", "falsified_if": "Failing devices do not have more frequent CE storm or error-burst events."}, {"id": "H8", "mechanism": "Log-transformed CE counts cap